To: sparclinux@vger.kernel.org, Linux Kernel list <linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org>

I just set up my E420R (4x450 MHx, 4G RAM). It worked fine with wheezy
current kernel but failed on power button-initiated poweroff with
3.7.0-rc5-00014-g9924a19 (mostly correct config below with some=20
drivers disabled since). The problem was not reproducible with this=20
kernel image (happened only once).

Startup and shutdown also worked fine with Debian-packaged 3.2.32.

There are may warnings and BUG-s and one OOPS at the end, then hang. I
do not know if there is something useful in here.

